cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Moving Trash Bin: a catching robot using gravity-constrained monocular trajectory estimation"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
abstract: >-
  An omnidirectional robot that catches thrown objects by predicting their
  landing point from a single upward-facing camera. A single image cannot
  recover depth, so the system uses gravity as a scale reference: the
  trajectory that a constant 9.8 m/s^2 acceleration would have produced is
  solved directly, which fixes the scale without knowing the object's size.
  The estimator is a single 2N-by-6 linear least-squares solve with no
  iteration, initial guess, or convergence failure, and it is corrected for
  the motion of the camera, which rides on the robot.
